verdict.suggested_fix:
In manufacturer_scope_components (src/quality/compliance/shared.rs:26-30), handle the degenerate no-roots case by falling back to all components, preserving the scoping fix for normal graphs:

```rust
let roots: Vec<&Component> = sbom
    .components
    .iter()
    .filter(|(id, _)| !incoming.contains(id))
    .map(|(_, c)| c)
    .collect();
if roots.is_empty() {
    // Fully cyclic graph (or no acyclic root): no component is provably a
    // dependency-only node, so fall back to scanning all components rather
    // than making manufacturer evidence unsatisfiable.
    return sbom.components.values().collect();
}
roots
```

(A more precise alternative is SCC-condensation roots, but the empty-fallback is the minimal safe fix and restores pre-83d9945 behavior only in the degenerate case.) Add a regression test: cyclic two-component CycloneDX SBOM with SecurityContact+Advisories refs must pass check_cra_oss_steward with no Art. 24 Error.
